{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said: I will blot out, etc.</b> It was necessary to say ״for I regret״ etc., and it was not sufficient with what He said in the preceding verse — this comes to say that the reason He said ״I will blot out״ is because He regretted having made them, not because of their evil deeds. For there is a difference: if the destruction were because of their evil deeds, those who did not deserve destruction would be found among them, and they are those who had not reached the level of punishment; but if the destruction is because HaShem regretted, small and great alike are included in the decree. Therefore He said <b>I will blot out</b> etc., <b>for I regret that I made them</b> — and for this reason none escapes. And therefore Scripture immediately says <b>But Noah found favor in the eyes of HaShem</b> — meaning, not because of his deeds, for in the aspect of the reversal — that HaShem turned back from the creation of man — his being righteous would not save him; therefore it was necessary to say ״found favor״ and not his merit. And from this there is no proof to say that he was not righteous, for even though he was righteous, his righteousness would not save him, but rather the aspect of favor that he attained through the intermediary of the aspect of the commandments. For you should know that there is a commandment whose effect is to draw favor upon a person, or in the aspect of three or four known commandments — and HaShem did not disclose the effects of the commandments, for the reason that the Sages, blessed be their memory, stated (Tanhuma, Eikev): that all the world would rush to [perform them] for their effects. And this Noah merited and found the favor; his name too declares this — Noaḥ [is] ḥen [favor] (נֹחַ — חֵן)." "<b>Thus concludes the portion of Genesis.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:39:32.285670674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}